    "custom_liquid_QMeCX3": {
      "type": "custom-liquid",
      "name": "t:sections.custom-liquid.presets.name",
      "settings": {
        "custom_liquid": "{% if collection.handle == 'golf-irons' %}\n  <section class=\"hw-iron-guide\" aria-labelledby=\"hw-iron-guide-title\">\n    <div class=\"page-width\">\n      <header class=\"hw-iron-guide__header\">\n        <p class=\"hw-iron-guide__eyebrow\">Iron buyer’s guide</p>\n        <h2 id=\"hw-iron-guide-title\">How to choose the right golf irons.</h2>\n        <p>Haywood golf irons span four distinct profiles: forgiving game-improvement irons, compact players-distance irons, forged cavity backs and muscle backs. The right model is the one that produces repeatable launch, carry and dispersion while giving you the look and feedback you prefer at address. Handicap can be useful context, but strike pattern and ball flight should lead the decision.</p>\n      </header>\n\n      <div class=\"hw-iron-guide__models\" aria-label=\"Compare Haywood iron models\">\n        <article class=\"hw-iron-guide__model\">\n          <p class=\"hw-iron-guide__type\">Game improvement</p>\n          <h3><a href=\"/products/sv-2-game-improvement-irons\">SV.2 Irons</a></h3>\n          <p>The most forgiving starting point for golfers who want easier launch, greater stability across the face and better carry retention on imperfect strikes—without an oversized look at address.</p>\n          <a class=\"hw-iron-guide__text-link\" href=\"/products/sv-2-game-improvement-irons\">Explore SV.2 <span aria-hidden=\"true\">↗</span></a>\n        </article>\n\n        <article class=\"hw-iron-guide__model\">\n          <p class=\"hw-iron-guide__type\">Players distance</p>\n          <h3><a href=\"/products/pd-1-players-distance-irons\">PD.1 Irons</a></h3>\n          <p>A compact, confidence-inspiring profile with speed and distance support. Choose PD.1 when you want more help than a traditional players iron without the size of a game-improvement model.</p>\n          <a class=\"hw-iron-guide__text-link\" href=\"/products/pd-1-players-distance-irons\">Explore PD.1 <span aria-hidden=\"true\">↗</span></a>\n        </article>\n\n        <article class=\"hw-iron-guide__model\">\n          <p class=\"hw-iron-guide__type\">Forged cavity back</p>\n          <h3><a href=\"/products/cb2-forged-players-cavity-back-irons\">CB2 Irons</a></h3>\n          <p>A forged players cavity-back that pairs a compact shape and clear feedback with added stability. CB2 suits golfers seeking control and shotmaking confidence with more support than a muscle back.</p>\n          <a class=\"hw-iron-guide__text-link\" href=\"/products/cb2-forged-players-cavity-back-irons\">Explore CB2 <span aria-hidden=\"true\">↗</span></a>\n        </article>\n\n        <article class=\"hw-iron-guide__model\">\n          <p class=\"hw-iron-guide__type\">Forged muscle back</p>\n          <h3><a href=\"/products/mb2-forged-muscle-back-irons\">MB2 Irons</a></h3>\n          <p>A traditional forged muscle-back profile for consistent strikers who prioritize direct feedback, precise trajectory control and workability over additional help from the clubhead.</p>\n          <a class=\"hw-iron-guide__text-link\" href=\"/products/mb2-forged-muscle-back-irons\">Explore MB2 <span aria-hidden=\"true\">↗</span></a>\n        </article>\n      </div>\n\n      <section class=\"hw-iron-guide__combo\" aria-labelledby=\"hw-combo-title\">\n        <div>\n          <p class=\"hw-iron-guide__eyebrow\">Combo sets</p>\n          <h2 id=\"hw-combo-title\">More support up top. More control down low.</h2>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"hw-iron-guide__combo-copy\">\n          <p>A combo iron set blends two compatible profiles through the bag. Longer irons can provide extra launch, speed or stability, while scoring irons deliver a more compact shape and direct feedback.</p>\n          <p><a href=\"/products/sv-2-pd-1-combo-iron-set\">SV.2 | PD.1</a> blends game-improvement support with players-distance performance. <a href=\"/products/cb2-mb2-forged-combo-irons\">CB2 + MB2</a> pairs the stability of a forged cavity back with muscle-back precision.</p>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <section class=\"hw-iron-guide__decision\" aria-labelledby=\"hw-decision-title\">\n        <div class=\"hw-iron-guide__decision-heading\">\n          <p class=\"hw-iron-guide__eyebrow\">What to consider</p>\n          <h2 id=\"hw-decision-title\">Choose for the shots you hit most.</h2>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"hw-iron-guide__criteria\">\n          <article>\n            <span>01</span>\n            <h3>Strike pattern</h3>\n            <p>If off-centre contact loses too much height or carry, begin with a more forgiving model. Consistent strikers can prioritize compact shaping and clearer feedback.</p>\n          </article>\n          <article>\n            <span>02</span>\n            <h3>Launch and gapping</h3>\n            <p>Compare average carry, launch and dispersion—not one unusually long shot. The best iron set creates predictable distances and useful gaps throughout the bag.</p>\n          </article>\n          <article>\n            <span>03</span>\n            <h3>Look and feel</h3>\n            <p>Confidence at address matters. Choose a profile you can aim comfortably, then configure the shaft, grip, length and lie to support your natural setup.</p>\n          </article>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <section class=\"hw-iron-guide__faq\" aria-labelledby=\"hw-iron-faq-title\">\n        <p class=\"hw-iron-guide__eyebrow\">Common questions</p>\n        <h2 id=\"hw-iron-faq-title\">A few answers before you build.</h2>\n\n        <details>\n          <summary>Which Haywood irons are the most forgiving?</summary>\n          <p>SV.2 is the best starting point when launch, stability and forgiveness are the priorities. Your ideal choice should also account for strike pattern, desired ball flight and preferred look at address.</p>\n        </details>\n        <details>\n          <summary>What is the difference between game-improvement and players-distance irons?</summary>\n          <p>Game-improvement irons prioritize launch, stability and forgiveness. Players-distance irons retain a more compact appearance while adding speed and distance support.</p>\n        </details>\n        <details>\n          <summary>What is the difference between a cavity-back and a muscle-back iron?</summary>\n          <p>A cavity back redistributes weight to provide additional stability on imperfect strikes. A muscle back uses a more traditional solid profile that emphasizes direct feedback, precision and workability.</p>\n        </details>\n        <details>\n          <summary>Can I try one Haywood iron before buying a full set?</summary>\n          <p>Yes. The <a href=\"/products/7-iron-purchase-program\">7-Iron Purchase Program</a> lets you order one custom-built 7-iron before committing to a complete set. Review the program page for current credit terms.</p>\n        </details>\n      </section>\n\n      <div class=\"hw-iron-guide__tools\" aria-label=\"Iron fitting tools\">\n        <div>\n          <p class=\"hw-iron-guide__eyebrow\">Still deciding?</p>\n          <h2>Start with your game, not a label.</h2>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"hw-iron-guide__actions\">\n          <a class=\"hw-iron-guide__button hw-iron-guide__button--primary\" href=\"/pages/fitting-tool\">Find my fit</a>\n          <a class=\"hw-iron-guide__button\" href=\"/pages/compare-irons\">Compare Haywood irons</a>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </section>\n\n  <style>\n    .hw-iron-guide {\n      margin-top: 88px;\n      padding: 92px 0;\n      background: #f2eee5;\n      color: #0b2341;\n    }\n\n    .hw-iron-guide *,\n    .hw-iron-guide *::before,\n    .hw-iron-guide *::after {\n      box-sizing: border-box;\n    }\n\n    .hw-iron-guide__header {\n      max-width: 850px;\n      margin-bottom: 48px;\n    }\n\n    .hw-iron-guide__eyebrow {\n      margin: 0 0 14px;\n      color: #c9a66b;\n      font-size: 12px;\n      font-weight: 700;\n      line-height: 1.2;\n      letter-spacing: .16em;\n      text-transform: uppercase;\n    }\n\n    .hw-iron-guide h2,\n    .hw-iron-guide h3,\n    .hw-iron-guide p {\n      color: inherit;\n    }\n\n    .hw-iron-guide__header h2,\n    .hw-iron-guide__combo h2,\n    .hw-iron-guide__decision-heading h2,\n    .hw-iron-guide__faq > h2,\n    .hw-iron-guide__tools h2 {\n      margin: 0;\n      font-family: \"Iowan Old Style\", Baskerville, \"Times New Roman\", serif;\n      font-weight: 400;\n      letter-spacing: -.025em;\n    }\n\n    .hw-iron-guide__header h2 {\n      max-width: 760px;\n      font-size: clamp(42px, 6vw, 68px);\n      line-height: .98;\n    }\n\n    .hw-iron-guide__header > p:last-child {\n      max-width: 800px;\n      margin: 26px 0 0;\n      color: #4a5568;\n      font-size: 18px;\n      line-height: 1.7;\n    }\n\n    .hw-iron-guide__models {\n      display: grid;\n      grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr));\n      border-top: 1px solid rgba(11, 35, 65, .2);\n      border-left: 1px solid rgba(11, 35, 65, .2);\n    }\n\n    .hw-iron-guide__model {\n      display: flex;\n      flex-direction: column;\n      min-height: 330px;\n      padding: 30px 26px;\n      border-right: 1px solid rgba(11, 35, 65, .2);\n      border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(11, 35, 65, .2);\n      background: rgba(255, 255, 255, .42);\n    }\n\n    .hw-iron-guide__type {\n      margin: 0 0 22px;\n      color: #8c734d;\n      font-size: 11px;\n      font-weight: 700;\n      line-height: 1.2;\n      letter-spacing: .13em;\n      text-transform: uppercase;\n    }\n\n    .hw-iron-guide__model h3 {\n      margin: 0 0 18px;\n      font-family: \"Iowan Old Style\", Baskerville, \"Times New Roman\", serif;\n      font-size: 34px;\n      font-weight: 400;\n      line-height: 1;\n    }\n\n    .hw-iron-guide__model h3 a,\n    .hw-iron-guide__model h3 a:hover {\n      color: inherit;\n      text-decoration: none;\n    }\n\n    .hw-iron-guide__model > p:not(.hw-iron-guide__type) {\n      margin: 0 0 24px;\n      color: #4a5568;\n      font-size: 16px;\n      line-height: 1.62;\n    }\n\n    .hw-iron-guide__text-link {\n      margin-top: auto;\n      color: #0b2341;\n      font-size: 13px;\n      font-weight: 700;\n      letter-spacing: .08em;\n      text-underline-offset: 5px;\n      text-transform: uppercase;\n    }\n\n    .hw-iron-guide__combo {\n      display: grid;\n      grid-template-columns: .9fr 1.1fr;\n      gap: 64px;\n      margin-top: 56px;\n      padding: 48px;\n      background: #0b2341;\n      color: #fff;\n    }\n\n    .hw-iron-guide__combo h2 {\n      max-width: 460px;\n      font-size: clamp(38px, 5vw, 58px);\n      line-height: 1;\n    }\n\n    .hw-iron-guide__combo-copy p {\n      margin: 0;\n      color: rgba(255, 255, 255, .78);\n      font-size: 17px;\n      line-height: 1.7;\n    }\n\n    .hw-iron-guide__combo-copy p + p {\n      margin-top: 20px;\n    }\n\n    .hw-iron-guide__combo-copy a {\n      color: #fff;\n      font-weight: 700;\n      text-underline-offset: 4px;\n    }\n\n    .hw-iron-guide__decision {\n      display: grid;\n      grid-template-columns: .65fr 1.35fr;\n      gap: 64px;\n      margin-top: 72px;\n      padding-top: 64px;\n      border-top: 1px solid rgba(11, 35, 65, .18);\n    }\n\n    .hw-iron-guide__decision-heading h2 {\n      max-width: 400px;\n      font-size: clamp(36px, 4.5vw, 54px);\n      line-height: 1;\n    }\n\n    .hw-iron-guide__criteria {\n      display: grid;\n      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));\n      gap: 30px;\n    }\n\n    .hw-iron-guide__criteria article {\n      padding-top: 18px;\n      border-top: 2px solid #c9a66b;\n    }\n\n    .hw-iron-guide__criteria span {\n      color: #8c734d;\n      font-size: 11px;\n      font-weight: 700;\n      letter-spacing: .14em;\n    }\n\n    .hw-iron-guide__criteria h3 {\n      margin: 18px 0 10px;\n      font-size: 18px;\n      font-weight: 700;\n      line-height: 1.35;\n    }\n\n    .hw-iron-guide__criteria p {\n      margin: 0;\n      color: #4a5568;\n      font-size: 15px;\n      line-height: 1.65;\n    }\n\n    .hw-iron-guide__faq {\n      max-width: 930px;\n      margin: 78px auto 0;\n    }\n\n    .hw-iron-guide__faq > h2 {\n      margin-bottom: 32px;\n      font-size: clamp(38px, 5vw, 58px);\n      line-height: 1;\n    }\n\n    .hw-iron-guide__faq details {\n      border-top: 1px solid rgba(11, 35, 65, .2);\n    }\n\n    .hw-iron-guide__faq details:last-of-type {\n      border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(11, 35, 65, .2);\n    }\n\n    .hw-iron-guide__faq summary {\n      display: flex;\n      align-items: center;\n      justify-content: space-between;\n      gap: 24px;\n      padding: 22px 0;\n      color: #0b2341;\n      font-size: 17px;\n      font-weight: 700;\n      line-height: 1.45;\n      cursor: pointer;\n      list-style: none;\n    }\n\n    .hw-iron-guide__faq summary::-webkit-details-marker {\n      display: none;\n    }\n\n    .hw-iron-guide__faq summary::after {\n      content: \"+\";\n      flex: 0 0 auto;\n      color: #8c734d;\n      font-size: 24px;\n      font-weight: 400;\n    }\n\n    .hw-iron-guide__faq details[open] summary::after {\n      content: \"−\";\n    }\n\n    .hw-iron-guide__faq details p {\n      max-width: 760px;\n      margin: -4px 0 24px;\n      color: #4a5568;\n      font-size: 16px;\n      line-height: 1.7;\n    }\n\n    .hw-iron-guide__faq details a {\n      color: #0b2341;\n      font-weight: 700;\n      text-underline-offset: 4px;\n    }\n\n    .hw-iron-guide__tools {\n      display: flex;\n      align-items: flex-end;\n      justify-content: space-between;\n      gap: 36px;\n      margin-top: 72px;\n      padding-top: 40px;\n      border-top: 1px solid rgba(11, 35, 65, .2);\n    }\n\n    .hw-iron-guide__tools h2 {\n      max-width: 520px;\n      font-size: clamp(34px, 4vw, 48px);\n      line-height: 1;\n    }\n\n    .hw-iron-guide__actions {\n      display: flex;\n      flex-wrap: wrap;\n      justify-content: flex-end;\n      gap: 12px;\n    }\n\n    .hw-iron-guide__button {\n      display: inline-flex;\n      align-items: center;\n      justify-content: center;\n      min-height: 48px;\n      padding: 14px 20px;\n      border: 1px solid #0b2341;\n      color: #0b2341;\n      font-size: 12px;\n      font-weight: 700;\n      letter-spacing: .11em;\n      line-height: 1.2;\n      text-decoration: none;\n      text-transform: uppercase;\n    }\n\n    .hw-iron-guide__button--primary {\n      border-color: #c9a66b;\n      background: #c9a66b;\n    }\n\n    @media screen and (max-width: 989px) {\n      .hw-iron-guide__models {\n        grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));\n      }\n\n      .hw-iron-guide__combo,\n      .hw-iron-guide__decision {\n        grid-template-columns: 1fr;\n        gap: 36px;\n      }\n\n      .hw-iron-guide__criteria {\n        gap: 22px;\n      }\n\n      .hw-iron-guide__tools {\n        align-items: flex-start;\n        flex-direction: column;\n      }\n\n      .hw-iron-guide__actions {\n        justify-content: flex-start;\n      }\n    }\n\n    @media screen and (max-width: 749px) {\n      .hw-iron-guide {\n        margin-top: 56px;\n        padding: 64px 0;\n      }\n\n      .hw-iron-guide__header {\n        margin-bottom: 34px;\n      }\n\n      .hw-iron-guide__header > p:last-child {\n        font-size: 16px;\n      }\n\n      .hw-iron-guide__models,\n      .hw-iron-guide__criteria {\n        grid-template-columns: 1fr;\n      }\n\n      .hw-iron-guide__model {\n        min-height: 0;\n        padding: 26px 22px;\n      }\n\n      .hw-iron-guide__combo {\n        margin-top: 40px;\n        padding: 32px 24px;\n      }\n\n      .hw-iron-guide__decision {\n        gap: 32px;\n        margin-top: 52px;\n        padding-top: 48px;\n      }\n\n      .hw-iron-guide__criteria article {\n        padding-top: 16px;\n      }\n\n      .hw-iron-guide__faq {\n        margin-top: 56px;\n      }\n\n      .hw-iron-guide__tools {\n        margin-top: 56px;\n      }\n\n      .hw-iron-guide__actions,\n      .hw-iron-guide__button {\n        width: 100%;\n      }\n    }\n  </style>\n{% endif %}\n\n{% if collection.handle == 'drivers-fairway-woods-hybrids' %}\n  <section class=\"hw-woods-guide\" aria-labelledby=\"hw-woods-guide-title\">\n    <div class=\"page-width\">\n      <header class=\"hw-woods-guide__header\">\n        <p class=\"hw-woods-guide__eyebrow\">Top-of-bag buyer’s guide</p>\n        <h2 id=\"hw-woods-guide-title\">Which Haywood wood or hybrid is right for you?</h2>\n        <p>Build the top of your bag around the shots you need to hit. Choose a driver for speed and forgiveness off the tee, a fairway wood for versatile distance from tee or turf, or a hybrid for easier launch and long-iron replacement.</p>\n      </header>\n\n      <div class=\"hw-woods-guide__models\" aria-label=\"Compare Haywood drivers, fairway woods and hybrids\">\n        <article class=\"hw-woods-guide__model\">\n          <p class=\"hw-woods-guide__type\">Speed and forgiveness</p>\n          <h3><a href=\"/products/adjustable-forgiving-golf-driver\">Driver</a></h3>\n          <p>A carbon-fibre crown, 811 titanium body, forged titanium face and 15-gram back weight support speed and stability. The adjustable hosel lets you tune loft and lie for the launch and flight you want.</p>\n          <p class=\"hw-woods-guide__best\"><strong>Best for:</strong> custom-built speed, adjustable launch and forgiveness across the face.</p>\n          <a class=\"hw-woods-guide__text-link\" href=\"/products/adjustable-forgiving-golf-driver\">Explore the Driver <span aria-hidden=\"true\">↗</span></a>\n        </article>\n\n        <article class=\"hw-woods-guide__model\">\n          <p class=\"hw-woods-guide__type\">Distance from tee or turf</p>\n          <h3><a href=\"/products/forgiving-fairway-woods\">Fairway Woods</a></h3>\n          <p>Available in 3-, 5- and 7-wood configurations, with a carbon-fibre crown, adjustable hosel and 15-gram rear weight for easier launch, stability and confident performance from the fairway or tee.</p>\n          <p class=\"hw-woods-guide__best\"><strong>Best for:</strong> versatile distance and a specific launch or carry window at the top of the bag.</p>\n          <a class=\"hw-woods-guide__text-link\" href=\"/products/forgiving-fairway-woods\">Explore Fairway Woods <span aria-hidden=\"true\">↗</span></a>\n        </article>\n\n        <article class=\"hw-woods-guide__model\">\n          <p class=\"hw-woods-guide__type\">Easier launch</p>\n          <h3><a href=\"/products/forgiving-golf-hybrid\">Hybrid</a></h3>\n          <p>A compact alternative to a fairway wood or long iron. Its mid-to-high launch, adjustable hosel and rear weighting help produce reliable height and distance with added forgiveness.</p>\n          <p class=\"hw-woods-guide__best\"><strong>Best for:</strong> long approaches and a more forgiving replacement for a difficult long iron.</p>\n          <a class=\"hw-woods-guide__text-link\" href=\"/products/forgiving-golf-hybrid\">Explore the Hybrid <span aria-hidden=\"true\">↗</span></a>\n        </article>\n      </div>\n\n      <section class=\"hw-woods-guide__decision\" aria-labelledby=\"hw-woods-decision-title\">\n        <div class=\"hw-woods-guide__decision-heading\">\n          <p class=\"hw-woods-guide__eyebrow\">How to choose</p>\n          <h2 id=\"hw-woods-decision-title\">Start with the shot your bag is missing.</h2>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"hw-woods-guide__criteria\">\n          <article>\n            <span>01</span>\n            <h3>Define the job</h3>\n            <p>Choose a driver primarily for tee shots, a fairway wood for distance from tee and turf, or a hybrid when easier launch and long-iron replacement matter most.</p>\n          </article>\n          <article>\n            <span>02</span>\n            <h3>Compare carry and gapping</h3>\n            <p>Prioritize repeatable carry over one unusually long shot. The gaps between your driver, fairway woods, hybrid and longest iron should be useful and predictable.</p>\n          </article>\n          <article>\n            <span>03</span>\n            <h3>Choose the right wood</h3>\n            <p>A 3-wood generally flies lowest and farthest. A 5-wood adds launch, while a 7-wood offers the highest flight and steepest landing angle for long approaches.</p>\n          </article>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <section class=\"hw-woods-guide__compare\" aria-labelledby=\"hw-woods-compare-title\">\n        <div>\n          <p class=\"hw-woods-guide__eyebrow\">Compare your options</p>\n          <h2 id=\"hw-woods-compare-title\">Fairway wood vs. hybrid vs. driving iron.</h2>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"hw-woods-guide__compare-copy\">\n          <p>A fairway wood offers a larger profile and more distance potential. A hybrid provides a compact shape, easier launch and a natural transition toward the irons. A driving iron produces a more penetrating flight for golfers who strike irons consistently.</p>\n          <div class=\"hw-woods-guide__articles\">\n            <a href=\"/blogs/news/driving-iron-vs-fairway-wood\">Driving iron vs. fairway wood <span aria-hidden=\"true\">→</span></a>\n            <a href=\"/blogs/news/2-iron-vs-3-iron-vs-hybrid\">2-iron vs. 3-iron vs. hybrid <span aria-hidden=\"true\">→</span></a>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <section class=\"hw-woods-guide__faq\" aria-labelledby=\"hw-woods-faq-title\">\n        <p class=\"hw-woods-guide__eyebrow\">Common questions</p>\n        <h2 id=\"hw-woods-faq-title\">A few answers before you build.</h2>\n\n        <details>\n          <summary>Which fairway woods does Haywood offer?</summary>\n          <p>Haywood fairway woods are available in 3-, 5- and 7-wood configurations. Each creates a different combination of launch, carry and landing angle.</p>\n        </details>\n        <details>\n          <summary>Should I choose a 3-wood, 5-wood or 7-wood?</summary>\n          <p>Choose the distance gap and flight your bag needs. A 3-wood generally flies lower and farther, a 5-wood provides more launch, and a 7-wood produces the highest flight and steepest descent.</p>\n        </details>\n        <details>\n          <summary>What is the difference between a fairway wood and a hybrid?</summary>\n          <p>A fairway wood typically has a larger head and more distance potential. A hybrid has a more compact profile and is commonly used as an easier-launching replacement for a long iron.</p>\n        </details>\n        <details>\n          <summary>Can a hybrid replace a long iron?</summary>\n          <p>Yes. A hybrid can replace a difficult-to-hit long iron when you need easier launch, added forgiveness and more consistent carry.</p>\n        </details>\n        <details>\n          <summary>Are Haywood drivers, fairway woods and hybrids adjustable?</summary>\n          <p>Yes. All three use adjustable hosels, allowing you to tune the club’s setup, including loft, lie and ball flight.</p>\n        </details>\n      </section>\n\n      <div class=\"hw-woods-guide__tools\" aria-label=\"Wood and hybrid fitting tools\">\n        <div>\n          <p class=\"hw-woods-guide__eyebrow\">Built around your swing</p>\n          <h2>Configure the club, then tune the flight.</h2>\n          <p>Choose your preferred shaft, grip and playing length, then use the adjustable hosel to refine loft, lie and ball flight.</p>\n        </div>\n        <a class=\"hw-woods-guide__button\" href=\"/pages/fitting-tool\">Find my fit</a>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </section>\n\n  <style>\n    .hw-woods-guide {\n      margin-top: 88px;\n      padding: 92px 0;\n      background: #f2eee5;\n      color: #0b2341;\n    }\n\n    .hw-woods-guide *,\n    .hw-woods-guide *::before,\n    .hw-woods-guide *::after {\n      box-sizing: border-box;\n    }\n\n    .hw-woods-guide__header {\n      max-width: 880px;\n      margin-bottom: 48px;\n    }\n\n    .hw-woods-guide__eye